.env
.streamlit/secrets.toml
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/

# Paid Odds-API responses — large, ephemeral, regenerate. Kept local so the
# repo (and Streamlit Cloud) stay small; the app defaults to reading whatever is
# here and only spends credits when you tap "Pull fresh props".
# To ride a props snapshot to the cloud for a $0 phone session:
#     git add -f data/cache && git commit -m "cache snapshot"
data/cache/

# Historical NFL/NBA player-prop pulls (2026-07-24, spent an expiring paid key's
# remaining ~90k credits on these -- see data/HISTORICAL_COLLECTION_README.md).
# ~70MB raw, same "large + paid + regenerate-if-ever-needed" logic as data/cache/
# above -- NOT regenerable for free though (that key is gone), so this is the
# only copy; back it up somewhere durable outside git, don't rely on this repo.
data/nfl_historical_props_*/
data/nfl_historical_events_*.json
data/nba_historical_props_*/
data/nba_historical_fantasypts_*/
data/nba_historical_events_*.json

# Free ground truth (nflverse / stats.nba.com) + the joined props+truth model
# rows -- UNLIKE the paid props above, these ARE regenerable for free anytime
# (scripts/nfl_ground_truth_collect.py, nba_ground_truth_collect.py,
# nfl_ingest.py, nba_ingest.py all stay committed) -- gitignored purely for
# size (59MB+15MB raw), same call as MLB's own data/model_lab_rows.json.
data/nfl_ground_truth/
data/nba_ground_truth/
data/nfl_model_rows_*.json
data/nba_model_rows_*.json

# Credit ledger + personal bet history — never publish.
data/odds_api_credits.json
data/clv_log.csv

# Pinned "my DK entry" CSVs (app.py Save button) — personal, per-day, ephemeral.
data/dfs_entries_*.csv

# Ignore generated JSON caches by default...
data/*.json
data/*.parquet
data/*.duckdb
data/bullpen_cache/
data/actuals_cache/

# ...but DO commit the free, non-sensitive model data so cloud cold-starts are
# fast and the hitter model keeps its park factors (the strikeouts path that
# park_runs used to read doesn't exist on Streamlit Cloud).
!data/park_factors.json
!data/dfs_skill_2024_2025.json
!data/dfs_pitch_k9_2025.json
!data/dfs_season_hitting.json
!data/dfs_skill_2024_2025_2026_eb60.json
!data/dfs_pitch_era_2025_2026.json
!data/dfs_pitch_k9_2025_2026.json

# Hand-maintained (not generated) — cash/gpp tag per contest export, needed by
# dfs_ownership_gamma_sweep.py. Would silently reset to "unknown" on a fresh
# clone/deploy without this, breaking the cash-exclusion logic it feeds.
!data/contest_meta.json

# Your DK entry history is your real financial/contest activity, not a public
# leaderboard like contest-standings-*.csv (those are DK's own public per-
# contest exports; this is your personal record across all of them) -- this
# repo is public, so it never gets committed. scripts/dfs_entry_history.py
# reads it locally regardless of git status. Matches any numbered re-export
# (...history2.csv, ...history3.csv, etc).
data/draftkings-contest-entry-history*.csv

# Pick'em: the backtest result IS committed (small, aggregate, no personal
# data -- same category as the DFS calibration JSON above), so it needs an
# exception to the blanket `data/*.json` rule.
!data/pickem_backtest_results.json

# Pick'em: your TOO-GOODE pool's standings, opponents, and $ splits, plus
# your own per-game pick log -- same "real financial/contest activity in a
# public repo" logic as the DK entry history above, so the whole local
# working directory stays off GitHub. pages/*_Pickem.py and
# scripts/pickem_weekly.py read these locally regardless of git status.
data/pickem/

# Pick'em: raw nflverse schedule mirror (2MB), auto-downloaded by
# edge/pickem_features.load_games on first use -- regenerable for free, same
# call as the other nflverse ground-truth files above. The DERIVED
# data/pbp_team_game.csv (small, aggregated) IS committed.
data/nflverse_games.csv

# Arbitrage snapshot: the Streamlit page reads this
!data/arb_snapshot.json

# Fanatics' Oddschecker league ids. Committed because rebuilding it means
# ~30,000 probes of a third party's API (edge/arb/oddschecker_discover.py) and
# the result is public, non-sensitive reference data that changes about as
# often as a league does. Without it the scan falls back to three hardcoded
# ids and loses two dozen leagues.
!data/oddschecker_leagues.json

# The phone's scan request. Tracked because it IS the message: the Streamlit
# app commits it through the GitHub API and scripts/arb_agent.py reads it off
# origin/main. Both need an exception to the blanket data/*.json rule above --
# the API ignores .gitignore, so without this the file would exist on GitHub
# and be invisible locally, which is a confusing way to debug.
!data/scan_request.json

# Local bookkeeping for scripts/arb_agent.py (which request it last handled).
# Per-machine, and committing it would make two desktops fight over state.
data/.arb_agent_state.json
